No idea what's going on.  I just tried my setup,
which works:

   Mac OSX 10.8.4
   64-bit R GUI 3.0.0
   i686-apple-darwin11-llvm-g++-4.2 (GCC) 4.2.1
   Stan 1.3.0 release version
      Rcpp 0.10.3
      inline 0.3.11

The main difference is a different version of g++.
The other compiler options may make a difference, too.

Here are the models I tried:

oob.stan
-----------------------------------------
transformed data {
   real x[2];
   x[4] <- 7;
}
parameters {
   real y;
}
model {
   y ~ normal(0,1);
}
----------------------------------------

and

oob2.stan
-----------------------------------------
parameters {
   real y;
}
transformed parameters {
   real x[2];
   x[4] <- 7;
}
model {
   y ~ normal(0,1);
}
-------------------------------------------

Then in R, I see this:

 > stan('oob.stan')

TRANSLATING MODEL 'oob' FROM Stan CODE TO C++ CODE NOW.
COMPILING THE C++ CODE FOR MODEL 'oob' NOW.
Error : INDEX OPERATOR [] OUT OF BOUNDS; index=4; lower bound=1; upper bound=2; index position=1; x

failed to create the sampler; sampling not done

 > stan('oob2.stan')

TRANSLATING MODEL 'oob2' FROM Stan CODE TO C++ CODE NOW.
COMPILING THE C++ CODE FOR MODEL 'oob2' NOW.
SAMPLING FOR MODEL 'oob2' NOW (CHAIN 1).
Error : INDEX OPERATOR [] OUT OF BOUNDS; index=4; lower bound=1; upper bound=2; index position=1; x

error occurred during calling the sampler; sampling not done

- Bob

