That's pretty much what my package does. The problem is making sure you are still in the space, it is indeed a hard problem. You can either reflect at the boundaries, then the running time goes up exponentially with the length of x, or you can pick a random direction and sample uniformly from the line connecting you with a limit of this space (where some of the inequalities are sharp). The second method is much faster, O(1) samples, but it gets stuck in corners, apparently. I think I'm going to try to do some parallel stuff.

