>
> I went through the user manual and mailing lists, and haven't seen this done... but just wanted to check.

That is the expected, albeit poor, behavior.

> The following works:
> data{
>
> vector[2] x[100];
>
> }
>
> ...
>
> model{
>
> for (a in 1:100){
>
> x[a] ~ multi_normal(mu, Sigma);
>
> }
> }

It would be much better to invert Sigma once before the loop starts and then use multi_normal_prec, like

model {
  matrix[K,K] Sigma_inv;
  Sigma_inv <- mdivide_left_tri_low(Sigma, Eye);
  for (a in 1:100) x[a] ~ multi_normal_prec(mu, Sigma_inv);
}

where Eye is defined as an identity matrix in the transformed data block.

> This does not:

Correct.

Ben

