We should expose the mdivide_left_spd function which is what is really needed here.  Not sure why it's not exposed right now, I probably forgot to finish the user visible parts.

That said, the code Ben provided might actually be a bit slower, depending on the size of Sigma and how many observations there are.  cholesky_decompose and inverse do not have explicit derivatives, so they fall back to the (much slower) Eigen code paths.

I would guess that:

Sigma_chol <- cholesky_decompose(Sigma);
for (a in 1:100) x[a] ~ multi_normal_chol(mu,Sigma_chol);

Cheers,
Marcus

