Hi Bob,

Thank you for suggesting the print function - I hadn't thought of that!

So my code is correctly transforming parameters/data, and the indexes are all working correctly in the likelihood loop. In my data vector for the MVN, occasionally one of the observations will be missing:
[1.#QNAN:0,3.5:0]
and sometimes both will be missing
[1.#QNAN:0,1.#QNAN:0]

Do I have to do further processing to get the MVN to work? It seems that the values of my missing observations "#QNAN:0" reflect the error I am getting when I run the model?

Thanks

Mark

