Subject: Invert every element of a vector
Message-ID: <Ej3f0IrqKu0.-jiqVfnAV_oJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/Ej3f0IrqKu0/m/-jiqVfnAV_oJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

It seems that in Stan 1.3.0 the / operator is not defined for a real and a vector, so in particular it is not possible to have:

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=0> y[N];
...
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> alpha;
...
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] mu;
...
}
model {
...
  y ~ neg_binomial(1 / alpha, 1 / (alpha * mu));
}

I was thinking to get around this I would define a vector of all 1s of the length I need in the transformed data block and divide my vector by this as follows:

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=0> y[N];
...
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] one_vec;
  for (i in 1:N)
    one_vec[i] <- 1;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> alpha;
...
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] mu;
...
}
model {
...
  y ~ neg_binomial(1 / alpha, one_vec ./ (alpha * mu));
}

Is that all correct, or am I missing something?

Thanks,
Ted

